## User Guide&#x20;

1. Application Introduction&#x20;

This application provides a simple way to use the random forest for Machine Learning modeling. Random forest is an integrated learning method that improves the stability and prediction performance of the model by constructing multiple decision trees and voting or averaging their results. It performs well in dealing with high-dimensional data, dealing with non-linear relationships, and solving the Overfitting problem. Users can import data, train models, adjust parameters, and perform prediction and visualization analysis. This guide will help you quickly master the application operation process.&#x20;

* Function Overview

#### Data Import:&#x20;

Support CSV, XLSX, XLS, TXT format data sets.&#x20;

#### Model Training:

* Function Overview

#### Data Import:&#x20;

Support CSV, XLSX, XLS, TXT format data sets.&#x20;

#### Model Training:

Use the random forest algorithm for classification or regression modeling.&#x20;

#### Hyperparameter Tuning:

Support adjustment of parameters such as the number of trees (n\_estimators), maximum depth (max\_depth), and minimum number of samples (min\_samples\_split, min\_samples\_leaf).&#x20;

#### Model Evaluation:

Support multiple evaluation methods such as cross - validation, accuracy, F1 score, and feature importance analysis.&#x20;

#### Prediction and Visualization:

Predict new data and provide visual results such as confusion matrix, ROC curve and feature importance map.&#x20;

