## Usage Guide:&#x20;

* Application Introduction&#x20;

This application provides an efficient and practical way to use the LightGBM algorithm for Machine Learning modeling. LightGBM (Light Gradient Boosting Machine) is a gradient boosting framework based on decision trees, which features fast training speed, low memory usage, and high accuracy, especially suitable for large-scale data and high-dimensional sparse features. The algorithm supports classification, regression, and ranking tasks, and natively supports categorical features, missing value handling, and parallel computing. This application supports data import, Model Training, parameter adjustment, and result visualization, making it suitable for developers to quickly build high-performance models.&#x20;

* Function Overview

#### ● Data Import

Support the upload and preview of common data formats, including CSV, XLSX, XLS, TXT, etc.&#x20;

#### ● Model Training

Default value: 31

##### ● min\_data\_in\_leaf

Minimum number of samples at leaf nodes to avoid overfitting.&#x20;

Default value: 20

##### ● feature\_fraction

Feature sampling ratio, used for the training of each tree, can prevent overfitting.

Default value: 1

#### ● Model Evaluation

Support multiple evaluation metrics and cross - validation methods to comprehensively evaluate model performance:&#x20;

* Classification: Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1 Score, Confusion Matrix, AUC/ROC Curve&#x20;

* Regression: Mean Squared Error (MSE), Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE), Mean Absolute Deviation (MAE)

#### ● Prediction and Visualization

Provide model prediction and intuitive display module, including:&#x20;

* **Confusion Matrix Diagram**: For Classification Result Evaluation

* **Feature Importance Plot**: Displays key features

* **Learning curve&#x20;**: Track the error trend of the model on the training dataset and validation set, and monitor overfitting&#x20;

