### 1. Application Introduction

## User Guide&#x20;

### 1. Application Introduction

This application provides a simple and intuitive way to use the AdaBoost (Adaptive Boosting) algorithm for Machine Learning modeling. AdaBoost is a boosting method that improves the overall prediction performance of the model by iteratively training multiple weak learners (usually shallow decision trees) and dynamically adjusting the sample weights. The algorithm has unique advantages in dealing with small and medium-sized data sets, improving the Model Generalization Ability, and anti-Overfitting. Users can import data, train models, adjust parameters, and visually analyze the model effects. This guide will take you quickly through the functions of this application.&#x20;

