## Usage Guide:&#x20;

### Application Introduction&#x20;

This application provides a simple and intuitive way to use the K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN) algorithm for Machine Learning modeling. KNN is an instance-based non-parametric supervised learning algorithm that measures the distance between the sample to be classified and the labeled samples in the training dataset, selects the nearest K samples, and makes predictions by voting or weighting. The algorithm is simple to implement and does not require a training process. It is suitable for classification and regression tasks, especially in small data scenarios. This application supports users to import data, train models, adjust parameters, and visually analyze model performance.&#x20;

* Function Overview

#### ● Data Import

&#x20;Support the upload and preview of common data formats such as CSV, XLSX, XLS, TXT, etc.&#x20;

#### ● Model Training

#### ● Feature importance analysis

&#x20;Analyze the contribution of each feature to the model in combination with Permutation Importance to assist feature screening and model interpretation.&#x20;

#### ● Prediction and Visualization

&#x20;Predict new samples and visualize the prediction results, including confusion matrix, learning curve, feature importance, etc.&#x20;

