### Help Document&#x20;

* Application Introduction&#x20;

This application provides an efficient and flexible way to use&#x20;**&#x20;ExtraTreesClassifier (Extremely Randomized Trees)&#x20;**&#x20;for classification modeling. ETC is an ensemble learning algorithm based on the improvement of random forest. By introducing more randomness in feature partitioning, it improves generalization ability and speeds up training. Compared with the standard random forest, ETC usually has higher computational efficiency while maintaining model accuracy, and is suitable for tasks with high-dimensional sparse data, large-scale data sets and more feature noise.&#x20;

&#x20;This application supports data import, Model Training, hyperparameter configuration, performance evaluation, and result visualization.&#x20;

* Function Overview

##### ● Data Import

&#x20;This application supports data import, Model Training, hyperparameter configuration, performance evaluation, and result visualization.&#x20;

* Function Overview

##### ● Data Import

&#x20;Support the upload and preview of common format data files (CSV, XLSX, XLS, TXT), automatically identify the label column and perform preliminary data processing.&#x20;

#####

##### ● Model Training

&#x20;Classification modeling is based on ExtraTreesClassifier. Compared with traditional random forest, ExtraTrees introduces more randomness in the feature division process of each node, making the model faster and less prone to overfitting, which is suitable for large-scale classification tasks.&#x20;

#####

##### ● Hyperparameter Tuning

* &#x20;The following core parameters can be adjusted: n\_estimators&#x20;

&#x20;Specify the number of trees in the forest. Larger values improve model stability and performance, but increase training time.

&#x20;Default value: 100

max\_depth

&#x20;Specify the number of trees in the forest. Larger values improve model stability and performance, but increase training time.

&#x20;Default value: 100

max\_depth

&#x20;Limit the maximum depth of the tree to prevent overfitting. If set to None, the node will split until the purity or number of samples in the leaf node is below the threshold.&#x20;

&#x20;Default value: 10

max\_features

&#x20;The number of features to consider when looking for the best split. Can be set to "sqrt" (recommended for classification tasks), "log2", or a specific integer value.&#x20;

&#x20;Default value: "sqrt"&#x20;

min\_samples\_split

&#x20;The minimum number of samples required to split an internal node. Setting a larger value makes the model simpler and more robust.&#x20;

&#x20;Default value: 2

min\_samples\_leaf

&#x20;The minimum number of samples required for each leaf node. This prevents some leaf nodes from making decisions based on only a few samples.&#x20;

&#x20;Default value: 1

