Subtitle 1. Oversampling: Provide options: RandomOverSampler, BorderlineSMOTE, SMOTE, SMOTEENN, ADASYN



Hint:&#x20;**&#x20;RandomOverSampler&#x20;**&#x20;: Randomly copy minority class samples until the class distribution is balanced.&#x20;**&#x20;BorderlineSMOTE&#x20;**&#x20;: Generate new samples based on the boundary of minority class samples, and generate synthetic data through interpolation method, especially focusing on samples close to the decision boundary.&#x20;**&#x20;SMOTE&#x20;**&#x20;: Generate new synthetic samples between minority class samples through interpolation.&#x20;**&#x20;SMOTEENN&#x20;**&#x20;: Combine SMOTE and ENN, generate synthetic samples and clean noise samples through ENN.&#x20;**&#x20;ADASYN&#x20;**&#x20;: Generate synthetic samples adaptively based on the difficulty of samples, and generate more synthetic samples for minority class samples that are difficult to classify.&#x20;

Subtitle 2. Downsampling: Options provided: RandomUnderSampler, TomekLinks, EditedNearestNeighbours

Hint: RandomUnderSampler: randomly delete samples of the majority class; TomekLinks: delete samples of the majority class that form "boundary pairs" with samples of the minority class; EditedNearestNeighbours: delete samples whose majority of K nearest neighbors are heterogeneous&#x20;



Subtitle 3. Hybrid Sampling: Provide Options**SMOTETomek**

Hint:**SMOTETomek**: Combine SMOTE and Tomek Links, generate synthetic samples first, then delete adjacent different category sample pairs to clean up the noise in the data.



