### Help Document:&#x20;

1. Application Introduction&#x20;

This application provides an efficient and intuitive way to use&#x20;**&#x20;PCA (Principal Component Analysis)&#x20;**&#x20;to reduce the dimensionality, visualize and interpret high-dimensional data. PCA is a classic linear dimensionality reduction method that can transform the original features into a set of mutually orthogonal principal components, sorted from high to low according to the amount of information retained (variance), which helps to reduce noise, compress data and visualize.&#x20;

This application supports importing data from multiple file formats, and helps users understand data structure, discover potential patterns and use them for subsequent modeling through standardized preprocessing, principal component extraction, visual projection and result packaging and export.&#x20;

