## Help Document&#x20;

#### 1. Application Introduction&#x20;

This application provides an efficient and intuitive way to use the KMeans algorithm for cluster analysis and visualization of data. KMeans is a classic unsupervised learning algorithm suitable for discovering potential grouping structures in data. It divides the data into several clusters through iterative optimization, and each sample is assigned to the cluster center closest to it, thereby minimizing the sum of the distances from the samples to the cluster centers (squared error).&#x20;

This application supports importing multiple data formats, and combines clustering execution, clustering label output and visual display to help users identify the internal structure of data and provide a basis for subsequent modeling and business decision-making.&#x20;

