### 2. Tree Diagram

#### 2.1 Components of the Dendrogram

* Leaf node: The bottom-most node, representing a single sample

* Branch: The line segment that links the leaf node or sub-tree, representing the merging of clusters&#x20;

* Branch height: the position on the vertical axis, indicating the distance between the two clusters&#x20;

* Root: The top, representing all samples finally aggregated into a large cluster&#x20;

#### 2.2 Interpretation of dendrograms

* Horizontal axis (X axis): sample&#x20;

* Vertical axis (Y axis): distance

* The lower the branch height: the more similar the merged samples/clusters&#x20;

* The higher the branch height: the less similar the merged samples/clusters&#x20;

