### 1. Application Introduction

This application provides a powerful classification modeling method based on the Multi - Layer Perceptron (MLP) neural network, a feed - forward artificial neural network that is particularly suitable for small and medium - sized structured data sets with non - linear feature relationships. The MLP model can automatically extract feature representations through multiple hidden layers and non - linear activation functions, effectively improving the accuracy of classification tasks.&#x20;

This application integrates the modeling process of MLPClassifier, supports multiple key hyperparameters such as custom network structure, optimization algorithm, activation function, and regularization strategy, provides multiple hyperparameter tuning methods including grid search, random search, and Bayesian optimization (Optuna), and supports visualization analysis tools such as cross - validation, learning curves, ROC curves, and SHAP interpretability.&#x20;

### 2. Function Overview

#### ● Data Import

Support the import of data files in a variety of common formats (CSV, XLSX, XLS, TXT), automatically preview the data, detect missing values, standardize the data and encode the categories to ensure that the data can be directly used for neural network training.&#x20;

#### ● Model Training

Neural network Model Training through MLPClassifier, the core functions include:&#x20;

* Customize the structure of the hidden layer and the number of nerve cells

