## Help Document:&#x20;

### Application Introduction&#x20;

This application provides a simple and efficient way to use&#x20;**&#x20;linear regression model (Linear Regression)&#x20;**&#x20;for supervised learning modeling, suitable for prediction tasks of numerical target variables.&#x20;

Linear regression predicts the numerical value of future samples by constructing a linear relationship between the dependent variable (target value) and one or more independent variables (features). It is one of the most basic and interpretable regression algorithms, suitable for scenarios where the features have a linear relationship, no serious collinearity, and Gaussian noise.&#x20;

This application supports users to import data, configure parameters of linear regression model, automatically complete model training and prediction, and visualize the model performance and prediction results.&#x20;

### Data Import&#x20;

Support file uploads in common formats (e.g.,.csv,.xlsx,.txt)&#x20;

### Model Training (LinearRegression)

The standard linear regression model implemented by sklearn is provided, supporting the following parameter adjustments:&#x20;

* Fitted intercept term&#x20;

* Positive coefficient constraint



### Model Evaluation

The following model evaluation methods are provided to comprehensively measure the model performance and generalization ability:&#x20;

* **Cross Validation (K-Fold)**: Support customizing the number of folds to avoid Overfitting.

* **Mean Squared Error (MSE)&#x20;**

* **Mean Absolute Deviation (MAE)&#x20;**

* **Determination Coefficient (R² Score)**
